      "claim_text": "\\label{eq:surface-presentation}\\] the fundamental group of the closed nonorientable surface \\(N_3\\). For a finite group \\(\\K\\), we place a \\(\\K\\)-label on each positively oriented generator edge of the Cayley \\(2\\)-complex and require the ordered product around every lift of the relator to be the identity. This is a subshift of finite type, denoted \\(X_{\\K}\\). When a finite-index subgroup \\(H\\leq\\LambdaSurf\\) fixes a configuration, that configuration descends to a flat \\(\\K\\)-connection on the finite surface cover associated with \\(H\\).",
