    {
      "claim_id": "P69-SEM-016",
      "claim_text": "<span id=\"rem:finite-recovery\" label=\"rem:finite-recovery\">\\[rem:finite-recovery\\]</span> Once \\(|\\K|\\) is known and there are \\(r\\) distinct degrees, the remaining reconstruction is finite. The rational function [\\[eq:moment-generating\\]](#eq:moment-generating) for \\((P_m)\\) has denominator degree \\(r\\); standard finite recurrence recovery determines it from finitely many exact moments. After its \\(r\\) bases are known, \\(r\\) even nonorientable moments and \\(r\\) odd nonorientable moments solve two Vandermonde systems. The infinite sequences in [\\[thm:reconstruction\\]](#thm:reconstruction) are used to state the invariant without assuming \\(r\\) or \\(|\\K|\\) in advance.",
